# The libraries' headers C++'s sysroot takes from the host's packages (bin/lib/repr-cpp/sysroot.bash's cpp_full_sysroot): not a
# toolchain's, each at the digest below (else left out, and said): fortify-headers' (Alpine's package of
# https://github.com/jvoisin/fortify-headers, 0BSD), which g++'s search list puts before musl's and which wrap musl's functions
# when _FORTIFY_SOURCE is set (g++ 15.2 predefines it on Alpine when optimizing: test/cpp/host/opt-deltas-gxx.edn).
# And linux-headers' (Alpine's linux-headers 7.2.1-r0, the kernel's UAPI headers, GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note: a program's use of
# the kernel's interface is not a derived work), the 16 files libstdc++'s src/c++11/random.cc reaches through <linux/types.h> and
# <linux/random.h> (_GLIBCXX_HAVE_LINUX_TYPES_H, _GLIBCXX_HAVE_LINUX_RANDOM_H), DECISION 411-1 (a): the runtime's unit by our route.
